From f6bcda3fc2c23d310ec73a6c224479cbbdcdcadc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 17:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/39] fix: stop the call-start flow flashing a screen that
 wasn't true
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Starting a call swapped the whole screen twice in under a second: hero → a
full-page "Requesting microphone access… Approve the prompt to begin." → the
call UI. On the common path the permission is already granted, so no prompt
ever appears — that middle screen was both a flash and a lie, and on an
auto-started call it fired without anyone having pressed anything.

The interstitial is now earned rather than assumed. Nothing changes for the
first 400ms, so a normal start goes straight from the hero to the call UI in
one transition. If startup genuinely takes longer, a neutral "Starting…"
appears; the microphone wording shows only when the permission check is still
pending after 250ms, which is the only time a prompt is actually on screen.

Because the screen no longer changes the instant Start is pressed, the button
stays live during startup — so start() gained a re-entrancy guard. Without it a
double-click would open two microphones and two sockets. Every early exit
clears the pending timers, including the previously unhandled case where the
access check itself throws.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MsbzieENuExjL1yUYc66vr
