From 486993801c4a4d3d9b27cf034b6ee0a3a3d36634 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 20:29:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/39] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20question-not-asked=20checklist=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?(M18=20=C2=A74.5)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five things a discovery call has to establish. The rep knows all five — what
they lose is track of which ones they actually covered, because they are
listening rather than auditing themselves. So this keeps the count quietly and
says something only at the end, when there is still time to ask.

Ambient, never an interrupt, which is the whole design. A checklist that
interrupts to say "you haven't asked about budget" while the buyer is
mid-sentence about budget is worse than no checklist at all. It fills in as the
call goes, and the one moment it speaks is when Stop is pressed.

Judgement calls, each with a test:

Coverage is STICKY. Something asked in minute two is still asked in minute
forty; un-checking as the topic drifts would make the strip flicker, and a
flickering checklist is one nobody trusts.

Covered items go MUTED, not bold — the eye should land on what is still
outstanding, which is the opposite of how a progress list usually wants to draw
itself.

The warning is silent when everything is covered, because a checklist that
congratulates you is noise. It is also silent when NOTHING is covered: that is
not a rep who forgot five questions, it is a call that was never a discovery
call — a demo, a check-in, a wrong number — and listing all five at someone who
never intended to ask them is how a feature gets switched off.

Stop is captured BEFORE stop() runs, since stop() clears the transcript state
the checklist was built from.

Scoring reuses the battlecard normalizer, so the contraction fix lands here
free. Precision over recall again: no pattern under five characters, and no
phrase shared between two items — a phrase in two places means one of them can
never be the reason a box got ticked, which makes the checklist quietly wrong.

19 tests. The semantic-coverage LLM pass the spec allows every ~45s is not
built; the keyword pass is the cheap 80% and it is the half that works offline
and instantly.

