The worklet now writes PCM into a SharedArrayBuffer instead of posting each
chunk through the renderer's main thread. A dedicated worker drains the ring
on its own thread and streams straight to the main process over a
MessagePortMain, so a render storm or long GC pause on the main thread can no
longer queue audio behind it — the mechanism behind the 90-second lag ratchet
(Deepgram accepts audio at only 1.25x realtime, so a stall doesn't cost what
it stalled, it costs 4x that).

Falls back to the original postMessage path whenever anything in the chain is
missing (no SharedArrayBuffer, no port, worker fails to start) — the fast path
degrades silently by design, so `--diagnose` now reports which route audio
actually took rather than which one it was supposed to take.

Lock-free SPSC ring: monotonic frame counters (not wrapped pointers) so
empty/full stay distinguishable by arithmetic; producer never touches the
read index; consumer skips forward on overrun instead of splicing two moments
together. Ring overrun is reported back as a gap marker, same as a shed queue.

Closes acceptance criterion 3.
