Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:11:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/39] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20zero-native-code=20mitigation=20f?=
 =?UTF-8?q?or=20the=20Windows=20endpoint=20bug=20(M18=20=C2=A77)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The real fix for the Windows headset-as-communications-device bug
(docs/windows-capture.md) needs the per-process loopback addon, and that is
blocked on repo write access to reach Windows CI. But the SYMPTOM needs no
native code: mic carrying real speech while the buyer channel is bit-exact
digital silence for a sustained stretch is the specific, nameable shape of
this bug, not an ordinarily quiet prospect.

BuyerSilenceWatcher (src/main/windows-capture/buyer-silence.ts) watches for
that shape on the existing multichannel stream — mic speaking >=15% of a 45s
window while the buyer channel stays silent the whole time — and fires once
per call. Wired into transcription.ts's per-frame ingest; the Live view shows
a banner with a one-click deep-link to Windows's sound settings (the actual
fix: set the same device as both Default Device and Default Communication
Device).

Ships today, on every existing Windows install, while the real addon stays
blocked.
