RecordingIndicator already flips to "you + the other party" the instant
buyer capture starts, but that only helps a rep watching the screen. A short
two-note chime fires on the exact false->true transition (never repeats while
already live, never on the way down) so a rep who glanced away still gets
positive confirmation that consent-gated capture is doing what the UI claims.

Not behind a Settings toggle on purpose — this announces a fact about capture
state to the person running it, the same category as the visual indicator
they already can't turn off.
