Subject: [PATCH 26/39] fix: bug-hunt findings from M18 workflow audit (12
 confirmed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audio ring/pump path (§1.4):
- worker.onerror/onmessage now stay meaningful after the handshake instead of
  closing over an already-settled promise resolver that silently no-ops —
  a post-ready worker crash now calls a real onFailure callback.
- recorder.ts wires that callback to send the worklet 'ring-detach' and drop
  its pump reference, so a dead worker actually falls back to the postMessage
  path instead of leaving the worklet writing into a ring nobody drains.
- awaitPort() now closes a MessagePort that arrives after the handshake
  already gave up, instead of leaking it (and the paired main-process end)
  until the next call.
- recorder.stop() sends 'ring-detach' before tearing down the audio graph.
- audio-pump.worker.ts reports ring overrun even while paused — it was
  swallowing dropped-frame counts during a pause that in fact overflowed.

Security:
- preload's re-post of the audio MessagePort now targets window.location.origin
  instead of '*', so it can't be delivered to a different origin's content
  were one ever embedded in this window.

Live view banners:
- buyerSilentWarning is now cleared on stop(), on any transcription error, and
  whenever otherPartyError is set or otherParty capture is explicitly disabled
  — it used to only clear at the start of the NEXT call, so a stale "buyer
  audio has been silent" banner could sit stacked above the saved-call banner
  or a newer, contradictory buyer-audio-stopped banner.
- transcription:captureLost (main's "no audio callback for 10s" signal,
  documented as "-> reacquire" but never actually wired to anything) now
  recovers the same way an unplugged mic does: end the session and surface
  the existing Reconnect flow.

Unrelated pre-existing bugs also found by the sweep:
- useTasks/useDeals: unmounting during the 6s undo window cleared the pending
  delete's timer without ever calling the real delete, silently resurrecting
  a task/deal the user had already been told was deleted.
- ApiKeysSection's "Saved" notice timeout had no unmount cleanup, unlike the
  equivalent timers in CrmSection/PersonalizationSection/AccountSection.
