sanitizeCommitments() (§4.7) were fully built and tested but had no IPC
handler, no preload bridge, and no UI — a rep had no way to ever run this
feature despite CLAUDE.md documenting it as shipped.

- calls-fs.ts: Commitment/CommitmentOwner become the canonical storage types
  (same pattern as CoachingReport) with `commitments?: Commitment[]` on Call;
  commitments.ts now imports the types instead of duplicating them.
  setCallCommitments() re-sanitizes at write time — the same defense-in-depth
  every other AI-derived call field gets. Deliberately NOT added to
  callBackupPayload yet: unlike coaching's scores/advice, commitments text
  hasn't been reviewed for what's safe to leave the device, so it stays
  local-only until that's a deliberate decision, not a side effect of adding
  a field to an interface.
- calls.ts: `commitments:extract` IPC handler, mirroring `coach:call`'s
  shape exactly (get call → run extraction → persist → return result).
- CallDetail.tsx: a "Commitments" card (same position/pattern as "Sales
  coaching") with a "Find commitments" button, loading skeleton, and a
  You-committed-to / They-committed-to split with due-date badges.
