MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Third and last of the further-improvements sweep's "dead feature" findings:
sanitizeGeneratedTrigger()/TRACKER_PROMPT (§4.8) were fully built and tested
in from-prompt.ts, but nothing ever called them — no IPC handler, no
persistence, no UI. A rep had no way to actually type "tell me when someone
mentions procurement" and get a working tracker, despite CLAUDE.md
documenting this as shipped.

- custom-trackers.ts (main): a small flat JSON file (custom-trackers.json,
  same pattern as sync-mode.json/app-settings.json — one blob, atomic writes,
  empty-list default on any read failure), with its own sanitizer re-run on
  every read regardless of who wrote the file. 11 new tests.
- live-cue.ts: `trackers:generate` calls the AI provider with a
  record_tracker tool and returns the RAW result — deciding whether it's
  usable stays in the renderer's sanitizeGeneratedTrigger, next to the
  Trigger type and the matcher it feeds, not duplicated as a second judgment
  call in main. `trackers:list`/`trackers:save` persist the renderer's
  already-validated list.
- CoachingSection.tsx (Settings → AI & coaching defaults): a "Custom
  trackers" card — a text input, a list of existing trackers with per-item
  remove, inline errors when a request isn't specific enough to pass the
  same precision bar as the curated starter library.
- useLiveCues.ts: custom trackers load once on mount and get merged into a
  fresh BattlecardMatcher alongside STARTER_TRIGGERS — well before any call
  goes live, since this hook is mounted with the whole Live Calls screen.

With this, all three features the sweep found built-but-unreachable
(monologue meter, commitment extractor, custom trackers) are now actually
usable.
