ngs option (records a real `pre-agreed` consent rather than bypassing one — `sanitizeConsent`'s hard invariant stays intact — off by default since only the rep can know they have standing legal basis); a fixed auto-start latch bug that made every detected call after the first silently do nothing; an earned-not-assumed startup interstitial (no more flash of a mic-permission screen that was never true); and a fix so an **auto-started call now actually ends and saves itself** (ambient detection's end-of-call signal was never wired to the thing that stops capture; the app-name-only detector had no end signal at all, so it now times out after 5 minutes of transcribed silence). **`--diagnose`** (§6) prints one block of text — version, platform, capture path, a channel self-test (a known tone per channel through the real interleaver, catching a rep/buyer channel swap that would otherwise silently mislabel a transcript), live session health, consent state, updater trust, and API-key presence — designed so a tester can paste one block instead of the app needing a live call to debug. **Verification:** `docs/session-health.md`, `docs/windows-capture.md`, `docs/security-audit.md`, and `docs/screen-share-safety.md` each separate what's actually been checked from what still needs a live service, a packaged build, or real hardware this dev environment doesn't have; `docs/acceptance-criteria.md` walks all 13 of the milestone's acceptance criteria with real measured numbers (not assertions) for the 7 fully verifiable in-container, including a `worker_threads`-based proof that a genuinely separate OS thread keeps running through a real 5-second synchronous stall on another thread (248/250 ticks landed inside the blocked window) — and honestly defers the rest (real Windows hardware, a live Supabase project, a live LLM key, two machines for cross-app screen-share verification) rather than guessing. A follow-up adversarial bug-hunt (19 agents) found 12 real issues in the new ring/pump path and elsewhere; 11 were fixed (a worker crash after handshake going silently unhandled, a leaked late-arriving `MessagePort`, stale UI banners that could stack contradictorily, `transcription:captureLost` being emitted but never wired to anything, plus two pre-existing bugs in Tasks/Deals where navigating away during the 6-second undo window silently cancelled the delete instead of completing it). A SEPARATE further-improvements sweep (6 lenses) then caught a real gap in three of the "live edge" features listed above: the monologue meter, commitment extractor, and custom trackers were fully built and unit-tested but had zero callers outside their own tests — no IPC handler, no UI, unreachable by an actual rep. All three are now wired end-to-end: the monologue meter renders next to the engagement gauge in Live Calls; the commitment extractor has a "Find commitments" card on the call detail view (persisted via `Call.commitments`, deliberately excluded from cloud backup until reviewed for what's safe to sync); and custom trackers get a Settings → AI & coaching card (create/list/remove) whose accepted triggers merge into the live `BattlecardMatcher` alongside the starter library.
 
