From 89178be122f9e83a238c3578040fbdf53747384a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:58:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/39] fix: accessibility gaps + parallel directory reads
 (further-improvements sweep)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Accessibility:
- CueControls.tsx: the sensitivity picker now reuses the shared
  SegmentedControl (aria-pressed, full Low/Medium/High labels) instead of a
  hand-rolled single-letter button group with no accessible state.
- LiveStates.tsx: the primary "Start live transcription" button (an icon-only
  circle) now has an aria-label — previously announced nothing to a screen
  reader.
- DealsView.tsx: the board/list view toggle gets aria-label + aria-pressed
  (was color-only, icon-only); FilterChip gets aria-pressed so its selected
  state isn't color-only either.

Performance — every list*() in the main-process file stores
(calls/tasks/deals/contacts/knowledge/events/objection-queue) read every
JSON file in its directory SEQUENTIALLY, one `await` at a time. Switched all
seven to Promise.all over per-file reads: each file's disk I/O no longer
waits on the previous one's, with identical skip-unreadable/corrupt-file and
sort-after semantics.
