From 0a0c2dcd121cc2df028f803ca9a329d170248dd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:06:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] fix: jump-to-latest, clip-button z-index, session
 health surfaced, onboarding key check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- TranscriptView.tsx: a "Jump to latest" pill appears once the rep scrolls up
  mid-call and disappears (auto-scroll resumes) once they return to the
  bottom or tap it — previously scrolling up had no way back except manually
  dragging back down while new words kept arriving underneath.
- LiveView.tsx: the "Clip this moment" button gets z-50 (was no z-index at
  all) so the cue/suggestion rail's z-40 can no longer paint over it and make
  it unclickable when the rail grows tall in the same corner.
- session-health-notice.ts (new, pure — kept out of LiveView.tsx specifically
  so it's unit-testable without dragging in LiveView's window-reading
  imports): session health was fully computed and streamed to the renderer
  every second but never shown. Folds into the EXISTING latency dot/label
  instead of adding a new element — a real problem (capture/socket dead, a
  shed or reset tier) now overrides the plain ms reading with a short label
  ("Reconnecting…", "Catching up…"); the common healthy case is unchanged.
- Done.tsx (onboarding): checks whether a Deepgram key is configured and
  shows a one-line heads-up before "Start my first call" if not — previously
  onboarding never mentioned API keys at all, so a fresh install with none
  configured would hit a confusing dead end on its very first action.
