From 4659143a683899cbcd2b9404eecfb8c02fd9af04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:17:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/39] perf: code-split every screen + the app/overlay entry
 point (M18 further-improvements)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zero code-splitting existed anywhere in the renderer: main.tsx statically
imported both the full main App and the ambient-detection DetectionOverlay,
and MainApp.tsx statically imported all eleven screens it can navigate to —
even though only one screen is ever mounted at a time (the render switch is
already keyed on `active`, remounting on every nav change). Every window paid
for all of it regardless of what it actually shows.

The detection-overlay window is the extreme case: a second, usually-hidden
BrowserWindow that loads this SAME bundle (main/detection-overlay.ts) with a
different URL hash to render one small floating card, yet parsed the entire
CRM/Calendar/Coaching/Analytics/Settings/Knowledge/Team/Live/PastCalls/Tasks
code along with it.

- main.tsx: both `App` and `DetectionOverlay` are now `lazy()`, so the
  overlay window's bundle no longer needs App's code at all (Suspense
  fallback is `null` — the overlay window is transparent by design, and a
  visible loading flash there would look like a bug).
- MainApp.tsx: all eleven screens (Home, Live Calls, Past Calls, Tasks, CRM,
  Calendar, Coaching, Analytics, Settings, Knowledge, Team) are now `lazy()`,
  wrapped in one Suspense boundary with a skeleton-rows fallback.

Measured: the main index chunk dropped from ~1.43MB to ~558KB; each screen
now ships as its own chunk (14KB-130KB), loaded only on first visit.

Also: Done.tsx (onboarding) now mentions automatic call detection and cloud
backup in one line — both are real, off-by-default features the onboarding
flow never asks about, so Settings was the only way to ever learn they exist.
